**Home › How You Are › Stress › Highly Strung**

Layer 0 — `src/ui/screens/Home.tsx:196-204` as it stands, plus two props:

    <Panel title={<Open subject={at('how-you-are', p.id)}>How You Are</Open>}>
      <p className="small">{wellbeingSummary(p)}</p>
      <Meter label="Energy"    value={p.wellbeing.energy} open={at('wellbeing.energy', p.id)} />
      <Meter label="Stress"    value={p.wellbeing.stress} open={at('wellbeing.stress', p.id)} invert />
      <Meter label="Readiness" value={readiness(p)}       open={at('readiness', p.id)} />
    </Panel>

Layer 1 — `src/ui/drill/drills/wellbeing.tsx`. Nine dials, not three. Depth here is exposure: sleepDebt, morale, condition, fitness, travelFatigue, nourishment and hygiene are simulated every day and appear on no screen in the game.

    defineDrill<Person>({
      type: 'how-you-are',
      resolve: (sim, id) => sim.universe.people[id],
      eyebrow: () => 'How you are',
      name:    ({ value }) => value.firstName,
      body: ({ value: p, open }) => (
        <>
          <p>{wellbeingSummary(p)}</p>
          {WELLBEING_DIALS.map((d) => (
            <Meter key={d.key} label={d.label} value={p.wellbeing[d.key]}
                   invert={d.invert} open={at(`wellbeing.${d.key}`, p.id)} />
          ))}
        </>
      ),
    });

Layer 2 — Stress. Prose first, then the two flows as openable rows. No arithmetic in the body; the coefficients are one `.hint` line at the bottom and nothing more.

    defineDrill<Person>({
      type: 'wellbeing.stress',
      resolve: (sim, id) => sim.universe.people[id],
      eyebrow: () => 'One of the nine',
      name:    () => 'Stress',
      body: ({ value: p, open }) => {
        const gaining = p.wellbeing.energy < 15;
        const held = personalityTraitsOf(p).filter((t) => t.systemMods?.stressGain);
        return (
          <>
            <p>{gaining
              ? 'It’s climbing. Below fifteen energy everything costs more than it should, and you’re at ' + Math.round(p.wellbeing.energy) + '.'
              : 'It’s coming down. Nothing’s adding to it — that only starts below fifteen energy, and you’re at ' + Math.round(p.wellbeing.energy) + '.'}</p>

            <Open as="row" subject={at('wellbeing.energy', p.id)}>
              Energy is what decides whether it climbs at all
            </Open>

            {held.map((t) => (
              <Open key={t.id} as="row" subject={at('personality-trait', `${p.id}/${t.id}`)}>
                {traitName(t, p)} — {t.cost}
              </Open>
            ))}

            <p className="hint">SLATE sheds 0.35 an hour, and a night’s sleep takes a good deal more.</p>
          </>
        );
      },
    });

Layer 3 — the trait. `personalityTraitsOf` is the only trait set in the game that still costs the player anything, and every one ships with a written `cost` string that has only ever appeared on the creation screen.

    defineDrill<{ person: Person; trait: PersonalityTrait }>({
      type: 'personality-trait',
      resolve: (sim, id) => {
        const [personId, traitId] = id.split('/');
        const person = sim.universe.people[personId!];
        const trait = person && PERSONALITY_TRAIT_BY_ID[traitId!];
        return person && trait ? { person, trait } : undefined;
      },
      gone: 'That’s not one of yours any more.',
      eyebrow: () => 'Something about you',
      name: ({ value }) => value.trait.label,          // "Highly Strung"
      body: ({ value: { trait } }) => (
        <>
          <p>{trait.description}</p>
          <p>{trait.cost}</p>
        </>
      ),
    });

**What the player sees at depth 3.** Three sheets stepped in from the right, Home still readable down the left, one dim across everything. The top sheet's header reads:

    Home › How You Are › Stress › Highly Strung
    Something about you
    Highly Strung

Getting out: press *Home* (one press, gone), or *How You Are* (one press, two levels), or the 26px strip left of the sheet that announces itself as `Back To Stress`, or Escape three times, or the backdrop.

**What did not have to be written.** Every number in that chain is already computed and already thrown away. Layer 1 is nine fields the model already ticks. Layer 3 is a `description` and a `cost` string already sitting in `src/engine/content/personality-traits.ts`. The only new writing is four sentences and the branch on `energy < 15`.

